ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain: a wire that keeps going back and forth over
the same seams is given up, and its faces stay as they are (mitcad#235).

The face merge builds the merged face's wires edge by edge; where no edge
left continues from the current vertex, it takes a removed seam edge there
(ReconstructMissedSeam). A thread whose turns meet in one edge, as the
bodies stored in files have them, leaves on a cylinder through the meeting
edges (the intersection of the threaded part with the cylinder of the
thread's crest, past the end of a blind bore) seven pieces of the one
cylindrical surface, cut by the helix and by lines along the axis that end
on it. Merging them, the wire went from a removed edge to the removed
seam and back again without end: in 15 s it held 1.5 million edges, and
it ran on until the memory was gone.

A wire runs along each edge left at most once and along each removed edge
at most twice (once each way along a seam), so a wire with more edges than
that repeats itself; it now counts its edges and is given up past that
bound, as when no next edge is found (isWireBuildingFailed): the faces are
left unmerged. Nothing changes for wires within the bound.

--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKShHealing/ShapeUpgrade/ShapeUpgrade_UnifySameDomain.cxx
@@ -4026,6 +4026,12 @@
         gp_Pnt2d CurPoint   = StartPCurve->Value(CurParam);
 
         TopoDS_Edge CurEdge = StartEdge;
+        // A wire runs along each of the edges left at most once and along
+        // each removed seam at most twice (mitcad#235): a longer one repeats
+        // itself, going back and forth over seams found again and again by
+        // ReconstructMissedSeam, and never closes.
+        const int aMaxWireEdges = edges.Length() + 2 * RemovedEdges.Length() + 1;
+        int       aNbWireEdges  = 1;
         for (;;) // loop till the end of current new wire
         {
           TopoDS_Edge NextEdge;
@@ -4242,6 +4248,12 @@
               break;
             }
           }
+          if (++aNbWireEdges > aMaxWireEdges)
+          {
+            // The faces stay as they are.
+            isWireBuildingFailed = true;
+            break;
+          }
           CurPoint  = NextPoint;
           CurEdge   = NextEdge;
           CurVertex = TopExp::LastVertex(CurEdge, true); // with orientation
